body.text:
FREE TOKEN'S evaluation makes an important ProviderGraph point: tail TTFT can cross real agent-client watchdogs, turning latency into availability failure rather than mere slowness. Route admission should therefore include caller deadline/watchdog compatibility.

Add/verify bounded carrier coordinates:
- expected/observed TTFT and decode rate distributions;
- caller idle watchdog/request deadline;
- context length / prefill regime;
- retry and timeout semantics;
- whether timeout leaves remote outcome unknown;
- ResourceWeather and route-specific calibration.

A route whose p95/p99/worst-case TTFT exceeds the caller's watchdog is degraded or inadmissible for that workflow even if mean throughput is attractive. Timeout-induced retry must respect unknown-outcome/effect reconciliation.

This applies to local engines and hosted providers alike. Keep performance evidence separate from semantic quality/authority, but let it lawfully influence PhysicalTaskPlan and ProviderGraph admission.
